# Answering the on-call session from Discord, which is off until both lines below have a
# value. Neither is a secret — a channel id is in the URL of every message in it and a user
# id is on Tim's own profile — so they are here rather than in 1Password, and the bot token
# that is a secret is a reference in hachiko.env.op beside the wrapper.
#
# channel: the private channel hachiko alerts to. Each incident gets a thread in it.
# user:    the one account a reply is taken from. Everything else in the thread is ignored,
#          the bot's own messages included, because a reply is an instruction to an agent
#          with authority over this Mac.
#
# Both are snowflakes: enable Developer Mode in Discord and copy the id.
#
# What else it needs: a Discord application with a bot, the Message Content intent turned
# on, invited to the server with permission to read messages, send them, create threads and
# add reactions; a `bot token` field on the hachiko-discord item in the dev vault; and an
# `approval` one-time-password field on the same item, which is the second factor an action
# on the never list needs. README has the whole of it under hachiko.

channel =
user =
